    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 197</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_197/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 26 Feb 2025 01:01:24 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_197/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    m := make(map[string]int)&#xA;    m[&amp;#34;qcrao&amp;#34;] = 1&#xA;    fmt.Println(&amp;amp;m[&amp;#34;qcrao&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;No.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;./prog.go:8:15: invalid operation: cannot take address of m[&amp;#34;qcrao&amp;#34;] (map index expression of type int)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/4W5-rMuIiYI&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;The address of a map element cannot be taken directly.&#xA;Once a map expands, the positions of keys and values change, and previously saved addresses become invalid.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 174</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_174/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jan 2025 10:15:27 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_174/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    s1 := []int{1, 2, 3}&#xA;    s2 := s1[1:]&#xA;    s2[1] = 4&#xA;    fmt.Println(s1)&#xA;    s2 = append(s2, 5, 6, 7)&#xA;    fmt.Println(s2)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;[1 2 4]&#xA;[2 4 5 6 7]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/XL6Vb0mzsEs&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;slices-sharing-underlying-arrays&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Slices Sharing Underlying Arrays&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#slices-sharing-underlying-arrays&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt; is initialized as &lt;code&gt;[]int{1, 2, 3}&lt;/code&gt;, its underlying array is &lt;code&gt;[1, 2, 3]&lt;/code&gt;, and both its length and capacity are 3.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s2 := s1[1:]&lt;/code&gt; creates a sub-slice of &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt;. At this point:&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s2&lt;/code&gt; shares the same underlying array as &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s2&lt;/code&gt; starts at index 1, has a length of 2 (elements &lt;code&gt;[2, 3]&lt;/code&gt;), and a capacity of 2 (original slice capacity 3 - starting index 1 = 2).&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;modifying-shared-elements&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Modifying Shared Elements&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#modifying-shared-elements&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s2[1] = 4&lt;/code&gt; modifies the third element of the underlying array (index 2). Since &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;s2&lt;/code&gt; share the underlying array, &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt; becomes &lt;code&gt;[1, 2, 4]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;append-triggers-reallocation&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;code&gt;append&lt;/code&gt; Triggers Reallocation&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#append-triggers-reallocation&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;When &lt;code&gt;s2 = append(s2, 5, 6, 7)&lt;/code&gt;, the original capacity of 2 is not enough to hold 5 elements (original length 2 + 3 new elements), triggering reallocation.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;After reallocation, &lt;code&gt;s2&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s underlying array becomes a completely new array, entirely independent of the original &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The elements of the new &lt;code&gt;s2&lt;/code&gt; are &lt;code&gt;[2, 4, 5, 6, 7]&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;s1&lt;/code&gt; remains unaffected.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
