    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 135</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_135/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Dec 2024 12:24:37 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_135/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;encoding/json&amp;#34;&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;type AutoGenerated struct {&#xA;    Age   int    `json:&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;`&#xA;    Name  string `json:&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;`&#xA;    Child []int  `json:&amp;#34;child&amp;#34;`&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    jsonStr1 := `{&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;: 14,&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;potter&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;child&amp;#34;:[1,2,3]}`&#xA;    a := AutoGenerated{}&#xA;    json.Unmarshal([]byte(jsonStr1), &amp;amp;a)&#xA;    aa := a.Child&#xA;    fmt.Println(aa)&#xA;    jsonStr2 := `{&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;: 12,&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;potter&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;child&amp;#34;:[3,4,5,7,8,9]}`&#xA;    json.Unmarshal([]byte(jsonStr2), &amp;amp;a)&#xA;    fmt.Println(aa)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A: [1 2 3] [1 2 3];&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B: [1 2 3] [3 4 5];&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C: [1 2 3] [3 4 5 6 7 8 9];&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D: [1 2 3] [3 4 5 0 0 0]&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: B &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/BRdAwDKfZt4&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 084</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_084/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:45:10 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_084/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code? Why?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    s1 := []int{1, 2, 3}&#xA;    s2 := s1[1:]&#xA;    s2[1] = 4&#xA;    fmt.Println(s1)&#xA;    s2 = append(s2, 5, 6, 7)&#xA;    fmt.Println(s1)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;s1 [1,2,4]&#xA;s2 [2,4,5,6,7]&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 043</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_043/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:21 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_043/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;encoding/json&amp;#34;&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;&#xA;type AutoGenerated struct {&#xA;    Age   int    `json:&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;`&#xA;    Name  string `json:&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;`&#xA;    Child []int  `json:&amp;#34;child&amp;#34;`&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    jsonStr1 := `{&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;: 14,&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;potter&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;child&amp;#34;:[1,2,3]}`&#xA;    a := AutoGenerated{}&#xA;    json.Unmarshal([]byte(jsonStr1), &amp;amp;a)&#xA;    aa := a.Child&#xA;    fmt.Println(aa)&#xA;    jsonStr2 := `{&amp;#34;age&amp;#34;: 12,&amp;#34;name&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;potter&amp;#34;, &amp;#34;child&amp;#34;:[3,4,5,7,8,9]}`&#xA;    json.Unmarshal([]byte(jsonStr2), &amp;amp;a)&#xA;    fmt.Println(aa)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A：[1 2 3] [1 2 3]&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B：[1 2 3] [3 4 5]&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C：[1 2 3] [3 4 5 6 7 8 9]&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;D：[1 2 3] [3 4 5 0 0 0]&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: B&#xA;Analysis:&#xA;When JSON deserializes, slices are handled by setting the slice&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;len&lt;/code&gt; to 0 and then appending data.&#xA;Because &lt;code&gt;aa := a.Child&lt;/code&gt;, both &lt;code&gt;aa&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;a.Child&lt;/code&gt; slices point to the same array. When appending to 6, since &lt;code&gt;a.Child&lt;/code&gt; had not yet expanded, modifying the underlying array was equivalent to modifying &lt;code&gt;aa&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rsquo;s data. However, when appending to 7, the &lt;code&gt;a.Child&lt;/code&gt; slice expanded and pointed to a new array.&#xA;Therefore, the data of &lt;code&gt;aa&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;[3 4 5]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
